DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssttrrlleenn() function computes the length of the string _s.  The ssttrrnnlleenn()
     function attempts to compute the length of _s, but never scans beyond the
     first _m_a_x_l_e_n bytes of _s.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The ssttrrlleenn() function returns the number of characters that precede the
     terminating NUL character.  The ssttrrnnlleenn() function returns either the
     same result as ssttrrlleenn() or _m_a_x_l_e_n, whichever is smaller.

